Understanding Edible Oils
Edible oils represent essential fats extracted from plant or animal sources, serving as fundamental ingredients across culinary and food processing applications. The market is dominated by vegetable-based oils (90% market share), with palm, soybean, sunflower, rapeseed, and olive oils being most prevalent. While these oils enable cooking, frying, and food preparation, health concerns regarding trans and saturated fats continue shifting purchasing behaviors toward healthier alternatives like olive and canola oils.
